  "completed_components": {
    "literal_lengths": "M_k=2^k, depth=floor(alpha*V_M/log 2), L_k=k-depth; natural subtraction is eventually legitimate, the fixed logarithmic band holds and L_k diverges.",
    "actual_intensity": "The actual (M-L)*2^-L intensity is between exp(alpha*V_M)/4 and exp(alpha*V_M), diverges for alpha>0, and has every fixed information margin for alpha<1.",
    "actual_window_ratios": "The literal rounded h/n ratio is <=4*tau*exp(-alpha*V_M) and is summable. Windows are eventually positive and satisfy 2h<=n. Then n<=2N, N+h=n+1 and h/N is summable.",
    "exact_normalization": "The actual site probability vanishes and h_k*2^-L_k tends to tau with the literal floor(tau*2^L_k).",
    "arithmetic_field_comparison": "The genuine signed full-field comparison applies to these lengths with error 10*exp(-nu_M)+4*M^(-1/6), whose dyadic sum is finite.",
    "empirical_corollary": "Corollary 7.8a: for each fixed alpha in (0,1) and tau>0 the genuine arithmetic empirical count masses converge almost surely in total variation to Poisson(tau). No final asymptotic or numerical-regime premise remains.",
    "displayed_window_growth": "Eventually (tau/2)*M*exp(-alpha*V_M)<=h<=2*tau*M*exp(-alpha*V_M); log(h)/log(M) tends to one. These substantiate both displayed window-growth claims in the corollary."
  },
  "literature_inputs": "The final empirical theorem retains the existing ordinary PNT, Laishram-Shorey, Nicolas-Robin and directional Stein solution inputs of the proved microscopic comparison. Its analytic solution premise is stated eventually on the actual retained coordinate rates at the literal lengths and information zero. The full-field bound, information budget, summability, site-rate decay and window-mean convergence are proved, not assumed.",
  "limits": [
    "The full-probability set is for each fixed alpha and tau on the specified dyadic scales; no simultaneous all-parameter or all-size conclusion.",
    "The fixed-realization full-field support obstruction 7.8b remains open.",
    "The analytic solution construction in F.2 remains an explicit premise, as in the baseline.",
    "Typical/affine dictionaries, information-adapted saddle and Palm/cumulant families remain incomplete.",
    "No new NanoDa/Comparator qualification or Palomar submission for these 321 declarations."
  ],
